-- title:
--   Kurosh-type bound for subgroups of a free product
-- statement:
--   Let $G_0, G_1$ be groups, indexed as a family $G : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathrm{Type}$ of groups, and let $G_0 * G_1$ be their free product, realised as the monoid coproduct `Monoid.CoprodI G`. Let $H$ be a subgroup of $G_0 * G_1$ of finite index, and let $K$ be a field such that for each $i$ the cardinality $\operatorname{Nat.card}(G_i)$, viewed in $K$, is nonzero; since `Nat.card` of an infinite type is $0$, this forces each factor $G_i$ to be finite of order invertible in $K$. Write $\varphi_i$ for the canonical homomorphism $G_i \to G_0 * G_1$, so that $\operatorname{range}\varphi_i$ is the image of the $i$-th factor and $(G_0*G_1)/\operatorname{range}\varphi_i$ is the left coset space, on which $H$ acts by left translation. Then the $K$-dimension of the space of additive monoid homomorphisms from $H$, regarded additively, to $K$ — that is, of $\operatorname{Hom}(H, K^{+})$ — plus the number of $H$-orbits on $(G_0*G_1)/\operatorname{range}\varphi_0$ plus the number of $H$-orbits on $(G_0*G_1)/\operatorname{range}\varphi_1$ is at most $[G_0*G_1 : H] + 1$.
--
--   This is a quantitative Kurosh/Bass–Serre estimate: it bounds the rank of the free part of a finite-index subgroup of a free product of two finite groups, in the form of an inequality for $\dim_K \operatorname{Hom}(H,K)$ together with the two double coset counts $\#(H\backslash G / G_i)$. It is applied to $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \cong C_2 * C_3$, in the companion statement about the subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2$ generated by the images of $S$ and $ST$.
